MedWet represents a unique platform in the Mediterranean for sharing information and technical capacities between institutions, scientists and civil society on wetlands management and conservation. MedWet was established to support countries in the Mediterranean region in their implementation of the conservation and wise use of wetlands within the framework of the Ramsar Convention on Wetlands. 

The main objectives are:
&bull; To promote and participate in the implementation of the Ramsar Convention&rsquo;s objectives and initiatives in the Mediterranean region;
&bull; To develop and reinforce the capacity of governments and civil society for the sustainable management of wetlands, especially those designated as Wetlands of International Importance under the Ramsar Convention;
&bull; To act as a catalyst for the exchange of knowledge and expertise between key conservation and sustainable use actors in order to reinforce Mediterranean wetland management; and
&bull; To collaborate with other international initiatives in the region and globally.

Ellinogermaniki Agogi (EA) is an educational organization of private law, officially recognized by the state. EA was the first Greek educational organization, which applied Open and Distance Learning in secondary level education in the year of 1993.
Since 1998, the organization has established a devoted department, the Research and Development (R&D) Department for the design, development and implementation of research activities in education, expanding the collaboration with Universities and Research Institutions across Europe. The R&D Department, which currently employs 13 full time researchers, acts as interface between the pedagogical research, the technological innovation and the school community.
Since its foundation, the R&D department has been actively involved in more than 11 European projects dedicated to Astronomy or Space exploration as well as many more which were partly related to these two fields. In 2012 EA worked with ESA&rsquo;s education department to intergrade ESA&rsquo;s interactive applications in the Go-Lab(https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/317601)platform. As part of the EU Space Awarenessproject(https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/638653)consortium, EA worked alongside ESA&rsquo;s education representative and numerous ESERO offices designing and delivering e-learning resources for educators and educational resources for students. Following Space Awareness, EA was also part of the SpaceEU project(https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/821832)in which ESA Education was a member of the advisory board. EA is familiar with ESA&rsquo;s educational content as it has been making use of them for many years not only internally in the school but also in the framework of EU projects and teacher training courses. EA also has a long experience in designing and organizing teacher training workshops and courses on Astronomy and Space exploration.
The work of the R&D Department also focuses on the following areas:
a) the development of methodologies and empirical research to investigate processes of learning and knowledge acquisition in various subject-matter areas (physics, mathematics, biology, history, etc.);
b) the collaboration with computer science departments and artificial intelligence labs for the development of computational models and AI learning systems;
c) the collaboration with Universities and private companies for the development and testing of educational software;
d) the design of technology-supported learning and e-learning environments.

SPICI srl &ndash; Company for Innovation, Cooperation and Internationalization, is a Hub for innovation that, operating as an international accelerator and center for entrepreneurship, designs and supports entrepreneurial development, intergovernmental programs for scientific cooperation, technology transfer and internationalization for startups, university spinoffs and innovative SMEs, and develops digital transformation solutions for enterprises and public administration.
SPICI is an active and interconnected part of the ecosystem of knowhow, digital academies and scientific infrastructures of the Technological Pole of the University of Naples Federico II and within this highly valued context, SPICI provides advanced services for the Italian and European industrial and research system (in particular for startups and SMEs), which include scouting, acceleration, digital innovation, technology transfer, finance for growth.
Leveraging on the extensive and consolidated experience of the founders, SPICI works to encourage the attraction in Italy and Europe of capital, talents and innovative projects, providing specialized consultancy and financing guidance services.
SPICI operates both, directly and through its partners on the entire life cycle of startups, from the business conception phase to development on international markets, supporting teams and companies in the process of:
&middot; information and guidance on business creation and entrepreneurial training;
&middot; animation and scouting of new business ideas and management of pre-incubation and acceleration programs;
&middot; accompanying the creation and development of businesses through tutoring, mentorship, coaching, team building, business development and management of incubation and co-working spaces;
&middot; accompanying access to risk finance (venture capital, business angel);
&middot; support for patenting and technology transfer;
&middot; support for the development of digital transformation solutions;
&middot; access to internationalization programs and initiatives.

SPICI, with the aim of supporting companies and public administrations in the process of digital transformation, operates its division FabriTech. It acts as a technological laboratory for the development of digital products &mdash; including softwares, mobile and web apps and physical products &mdash; and related organizational solutions which impact on the way the organization operates internally and within the market.
SPICI has managed several programs related to business acceleration, among these, there is the &ldquo;CHINA-ITALY BEST STARTUP SHOWCASE - ENTREPRENEURSHIP COMPETITION&rdquo; the bilateral platform aimed at promoting the internationalization of Italian and Chinese innovative enterprises (startups, spinoffs, SMEs) that offers the opportunity to get close, approach, do business and land in the two Countries and to meet investors, incubators, science parks and partners through an intense and qualified networking activity.

Innovation experience HUB (innexHUB), Digital Innovation Hub of East Lombardy, was established in July 2017 as a non-profit association by the Industrial Associations of Brescia, Cremona and Mantova and two craftmanship associations located in Brescia. The aim was to create a subject focused on spreading the digital culture among SMEs, making them aware of: what being digital means, what KETs are, how the digital is rapidly transforming business models and the current and future opportunities / threats linked to digital technologies.
innexHUB has two additional purposes: to help enterprises understand their digital maturity level and identify the subsequent actions to digitally evolve as well as to guide enterprises in their digital transformation paths, ensuring they can rely on trustworthy suppliers.
During 2017 and 2018 innexHUB strengthened its governance by engaging with 6 new shareholders (associations and confederations) representing 3 additional sectors: Agriculture, Construction and Commerce, Tourism and Hospitality Services. As of now innexHUB action field encompasses and addresses 4 sectors (Industry; Agriculture; Construction; Commerce, Tourism and Hospitality Services) as well as 1 horizontal cluster (Craftmanship) made of micro and small enterprises across different sectors.
It is worthy to mention that 2 Universities figure among innexHUB shareholders and their technical and scientific contribution is essential for the hubs&rsquo; governance and orientation (e.g., representatives from both Universities have a seat in the hub&rsquo;s Technical and Scientific Committee).
Altogether innexHUB partners (shareholders) represent more than 50.000 SMEs located in the provinces of Brescia, Cremona and Mantova, equalling a third of the total population of active enterprises in the three provinces listed above.
In 2018 innexHUB has become fully operational by developing a catalogue of services that includes:
&bull; Awareness creation: design and organization of seminars and workshops centred around the increasing role and opportunities of KETs and digitalization as well as the provision and dissemination of information / materials (e.g. videos and reports on best practices / success cases) by means of the hub&rsquo;s website, e-learning platform and social channels;
&bull; Digital Maturity assessment: development and administration of digital maturity / readiness assessments, both in self-assisted (freely accessible web-based application) and assisted modes (on premises interviews), to evaluate an enterprise current state of digital readiness (i.e., processes, products, tools, skills) and identify possible evolutionary trajectories;
&bull; Ecosystem building, scouting, brokerage, networking: development of a catalogue of certified suppliers providing technical consulting in the design and implementation of digitalization projects as well as continuous training and education opportunities around digital topics to boost workforce upskilling;
&bull; Access to funding: dissemination of digital innovation funding opportunities and support to SMEs in accessing to public and private funding instruments;
&bull; Mentoring: support prior and during the implementation of digital transformation projects;
&bull; Education and skills development: co-creation, in partnership with external organizations, of training and education courses providing intelligence on SMEs&rsquo; needs and how to better address them.

Confindustria Brescia was founded on the 14th of April 1897. It is the oldest Italian entrepreneurial organization, having been active for over 110 years. As part of the Confindustria system, the Association represents the industrial and services sectors in the province of Brescia in all the political, institutional, administrative and trade union bodies, both local and national, in order to safeguard their interests.
This Representation is coordinated with other trade associations operating in the province of Brescia to protect the general interests of industry and the competitiveness of the economy of Brescia.
Confindustria Brescia now brings together more than 1,300 large, small and medium-sized enterprises operating in different sectors and employing a labour force of over 67,000 people.

Mission and objectives
The main mission of the Confindustria Brescia is to support entrepreneurial culture, to promote the development of the area. Members of the Confindustria Brescia can be industrial firms and consortiums producing goods and offering services.
The main objectives of the Confindustria Brescia are:
&middot; to encourage the spreading of entrepreneurial culture to develop the local economy through the promotion of innovation, the high quality of products and the improvement of production processes.
&middot; to pursue sustainable growth of industrial activities by providing assistance, consulting, and training courses to companies.
&middot; to develop competitiveness and the international aspect of industry in the area of Brescia.
&middot; to promote a closer link between education and the production system.
&middot; to assist the growth of employment and enhance the qualification of the workforce through training courses.
&middot; to contribute to improving the local infrastructure facilities. 
&middot; to strengthen interaction with local institutions and trade unions in order to develop the industrial framework of the province of Brescia along with the competitiveness of all firms.

Services
The Association, with all its various operational areas, offers services in crucial areas forentrepreneurial activities:
&middot; Relations with trade unions; 
&middot; Human resources management; 
&middot; Labour standards and norms; 
&middot; Safety and the environment; 
